# Effect Days 2025: Building Effect 4

Michael describes Effect 4 as a review of choices made in Effect 3, driven by production feedback. The work aims to remove duplicate concepts, reduce bundle size, and improve core data types. [04:21](https://youtu.be/nyvB6nRe5x0?t=261) [05:09](https://youtu.be/nyvB6nRe5x0?t=309) [06:17](https://youtu.be/nyvB6nRe5x0?t=377)

A fiber is independently running work. Batching groups operations. Transactional operations commit together.

He connects faster fibers with batching and transactional operations becoming ordinary Effect facilities rather than separate execution models. [22:56](https://youtu.be/nyvB6nRe5x0?t=1376) [28:03](https://youtu.be/nyvB6nRe5x0?t=1683)
